// D371 (`#prelude(...)` partial opt-in module attribute, Plan 62.F) —
// regression for [M-vec-access-e7320-as-bytes-str]: a consumer that opts
// into `#prelude(collections)` alone must still compile. The `collections`
// prelude facade (std/prelude/collections.nv) unconditionally re-exports
// `StringBuilder`/`WriteBuffer`/`ReadBuffer`, whose `#no_prelude` Nova-body
// implementations (std/runtime/{string_builder,write_buffer,read_buffer}.nv)
// call `str.@bytes()`, `char.try_from()`/`u8.try_from()` and construct
// `ReadBufferError`/`UnexpectedEnd` — all of which assumed a FULL
// `std.prelude` was already merged into the CU. Under this partial-prelude
// scope those symbols were never brought in, so the moment `collections`
// pulled the buffer/builder types into the CU, codegen hit `[E7320] no
// field or method as_bytes on type str` (checker level) and later
// `use of undeclared identifier 'CharTryFromError'` (C-codegen level, one
// hop deeper via char.try_from). Fixed by making the `collections` facade
// bring in its own re-exports' transitive deps explicitly
// (`std.runtime.string`, `std.runtime.char`,
// `std.prelude.errors.{CharTryFromError, TryFromCharError, ReadBufferError,
// UnexpectedEnd}`).
//
// Own subdirectory (NOT the shared `spec_tests.conformance` folder-module
// used by every top-level file in `spec_tests/conformance/`): `#prelude(...)`
// is a whole-compile-unit attribute — a differently-named module dropped
// directly into the top-level directory breaks the test-runner's
// same-directory folder-module peer detection for the OTHER 181 files
// (empirically confirmed: it turns every one of them into a
// `E_D78_MODULE_PATH_MISMATCH` CODEGEN-FAIL). A fresh, single-file
// subdirectory keeps this test isolated while still living under
// `spec_tests/conformance/` per convention. D29 `parent.target` naming:
// `partial_prelude.<file-stem>`.
//
// `#prelude(core, runtime, collections, protocols)` — the EXACT partial set
// the marker was found with (matches every peer of std/collections/vec/,
// the module that first exposed this bug). `core`/`runtime` are needed for
// `assert`/`Option` in this file's own test body; `protocols` is needed
// transitively — `std.runtime.string` (brought in by the `collections`
// facade fix) imports `std.collections.vec.{Vec}`, and merging vec's
// folder-module pulls in `mutate.nv`'s `AsSlice[T]` bound (std/prelude/
// protocols.nv). That transitive `protocols` requirement is a SEPARATE,
// wider gap in the same family (any `#prelude(collections)`-only consumer
// hits it too) — tracked by [M-partial-prelude-primitive-method-registry],
// not fixed here; using the 4-name set keeps this regression test scoped to
// the as_bytes/char.try_from defect this changeset actually fixes.
#prelude(core, runtime, collections, protocols)
module partial_prelude.d371_partial_prelude_collections

test "partial prelude(collections) привозит зависимости своих хелперов" {
    assert(1 + 1 == 2)
}
